.TH "pocket_trk" "1" "" "" "Pocket SDR"
.SH NAME
pocket_trk \- GNSS signal tracking, nav decoding, and PVT generation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
pocket_trk [\-sig sig \-prn prn[,...] [\-rfch ch[,...]] ...]
           [\-fmt {INT8|INT8X2|RAW8|RAW16|RAW16I|RAW32|CS8|CS16}]
           [\-f freq] [\-fo freq[,...]] [\-IQ {1|2}[,...]] [\-bits {2|3}[,...]]
           [\-toff toff] [\-tscale scale] [\-ti tint]
           [\-p bus[,port]] [\-c conf_file]
           [\-driver name] [\-gain gain] [\-bw bw] [\-gpio val] [\-EXT_CLOCK]
           [\-NO_SYNC] [\-fd dopp] [\-log path] [\-nmea path] [\-rtcm path] [\-raw path] ...
           [\-arch nch] [\-geom file] [\-sens name[,...]]
           [\-h height] [\-opt file] [\-debug file] [\-v] [file]
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Search and track GNSS signals in input digital IF data, extract observation data, decode navigation data, and generate PVT solutions.
Observation and navigation data can be streamed as RTCM3, PVT solutions as NMEA, and raw IF data and event logs can be streamed independently.
The output stream options \f[CR]\-log\f[R], \f[CR]\-nmea\f[R], \f[CR]\-rtcm\f[R], and \f[CR]\-raw\f[R] may each be specified multiple times, up to 8 output streams in total; each occurrence opens an
additional stream of that type (e.g., \f[CR]\-nmea sol.nmea \-nmea :2001\f[R] outputs NMEA to a file and a TCP server simultaneously).
.PP
The input can be a local file, a TCP stream, a Pocket SDR FE device, or a SoapySDR\-supported device (LimeSDR, HackRF, RTL\-SDR, \&...).
If the file path is omitted and \f[CR]\-driver\f[R] is not specified, the input is taken from a Pocket SDR FE device directly.
For file inputs, if \f[CR]<file>.tag\f[R] exists the IF format, sampling rate, LO frequencies, and per\-CH sampling types are auto\-configured from the tag, and the corresponding \f[CR]\-fmt\f[R],
\f[CR]\-f\f[R], \f[CR]\-fo\f[R], and \f[CR]\-IQ\f[R] options are ignored.
.SH OPTIONS ([]: DEFAULT)
.TP
\f[CR]\-sig sig \-prn prn[,...] [\-rfch ch[,...]] ...\f[R]
GNSS signal type ID (\f[CR]L1CA\f[R], \f[CR]L2CM\f[R], \&...)
and PRN list.
PRNs are comma\-separated and may use ranges (e.g.\ \f[CR]1\-32\f[R]).
For GLONASS FDMA signals (\f[CR]G1CA\f[R], \f[CR]G2CA\f[R]), the PRN is treated as the FCN.
\- \f[CR]\-rfch\f[R] assigns the signal to specific RF channel(s) (comma\- or \f[CR]\-\f[R]\-separated).
Without \f[CR]\-rfch\f[R], the RF channel is auto\-selected.
The whole \f[CR]\-sig\f[R]/\f[CR]\-prn\f[R]/\f[CR]\-rfch\f[R] triple may be repeated to track multiple signal types.
.TP
\f[CR]\-fmt {INT8|INT8X2|RAW8|RAW16|RAW16I|RAW32|CS8|CS16}\f[R]
Input IF data format.
\f[CR]INT8\f[R] = int8 (I), \f[CR]INT8X2\f[R] = interleaved int8 (IQ), \f[CR]RAW8/16/32\f[R] = Pocket SDR FE 2/4/8CH packed raw, \f[CR]RAW16I\f[R] = Spider SDR FE packed raw (8CH),
\f[CR]CS8\f[R]/\f[CR]CS16\f[R] = SoapySDR complex int8/int16.
[\f[CR]INT8X2\f[R]]
.TP
\f[CR]\-f freq\f[R]
Sampling frequency of the IF data in MHz.
[\f[CR]12.0\f[R]]
.TP
\f[CR]\-fo freq[,...]\f[R]
LO frequency for each RF channel in MHz, comma\-separated.
With \f[CR]RAW8/16/32\f[R], 2/4/8 frequencies are required.
With \f[CR]\-driver\f[R], these are the SoapySDR RF center frequencies of the RF channels and the first one is required; a channel with an omitted or \f[CR]0\f[R] frequency uses the first one.
.TP
\f[CR]\-IQ {1|2}[,...]\f[R]
Per\-RF\-CH sampling type: \f[CR]1\f[R] = I, \f[CR]2\f[R] = IQ.
Used with \f[CR]RAW8/16/32\f[R].
[\f[CR]2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2\f[R]]
.TP
\f[CR]\-bits {2|3}[,...]\f[R]
Per\-RF\-CH sample bit width (2 or 3).
Used with \f[CR]RAW8/16/32\f[R] when \f[CR]\-IQ\f[R] is \f[CR]1\f[R] (I\-sampling).
[\f[CR]2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2\f[R]]
.TP
\f[CR]\-toff toff\f[R]
Time offset from the start of the IF data in s.
[\f[CR]0.0\f[R]]
.TP
\f[CR]\-tscale scale\f[R]
Replay time scale for file inputs.
[\f[CR]1.0\f[R]]
.TP
\f[CR]\-ti tint\f[R]
Update interval of the runtime tracking status in s.
\f[CR]0\f[R] suppresses the status display.
[\f[CR]0.1\f[R]]
.TP
\f[CR]\-p bus[,port]\f[R]
USB bus and port number of the Pocket SDR FE device, when input is from the device.
.TP
\f[CR]\-c conf_file\f[R]
Configure the Pocket SDR FE device with a \f[CR]pocket_conf\f[R]\-format file before tracking starts.
.TP
\f[CR]\-driver name\f[R]
SoapySDR driver name (\f[CR]lime\f[R], \f[CR]hackrf\f[R], \f[CR]rtlsdr\f[R], \f[CR]sdrplay\f[R], \f[CR]bladerf\f[R], \&...).
Selects a SoapySDR device as the input.
Multiple devices are specified as specs separated by \f[CR];\f[R], and \f[CR]nchan=<n>\f[R] in a spec selects the number of RX channels of the device (default 1), up to 8 RF channels in total.
With multiple devices the external clock and time sources are selected and the streams are started at a common time latched by a 1PPS, so a common 10 MHz and 1PPS have to be distributed to the
devices.
The RF channels are then handled like the RF channels of a multi\-CH frontend, including \f[CR]\-RFCH\f[R] assignment and \f[CR]\-arch\f[R] array combining.
.TP
\f[CR]\-gain gain\f[R]
SoapySDR overall gain in dB.
.TP
\f[CR]\-bw bw\f[R]
SoapySDR analog filter bandwidth in MHz.
.TP
\f[CR]\-gpio val\f[R]
Output \f[CR]val\f[R] (0\-255) to the GPIO pins of the SoapySDR device (USRP: front\-panel GPIO).
The pins are set to outputs at the device open.
.TP
\f[CR]\-EXT_CLOCK\f[R]
Select the external clock source of the SoapySDR device.
.TP
\f[CR]\-NO_SYNC\f[R]
With multiple SoapySDR devices, do not synchronize the device times by a 1PPS.
The devices run on their own clocks and the RF channels of different devices are NOT aligned in samples (for non\-coherent uses such as a band per device).
.TP
\f[CR]\-fd dopp\f[R]
Maximum Doppler frequency to search signals in Hz.
Overrides the \f[CR]max_dop\f[R] key in \f[CR]\-opt file\f[R] if both are given.
[from \f[CR]\-opt file\f[R] or default \f[CR]5000\f[R]]
.TP
\f[CR]\-log path\f[R]
Output stream path for the tracking log (observation, navigation, PVT, events).
May be specified multiple times to open multiple log streams (max 8 output streams in total including \f[CR]\-nmea\f[R], \f[CR]\-rtcm\f[R], and \f[CR]\-raw\f[R]).
The stream path is one of: \- \f[CR](1)\f[R] local file path without \f[CR]:\f[R].
Time keywords (\f[CR]%Y\f[R], \f[CR]%m\f[R], \f[CR]%d\f[R], \f[CR]%h\f[R], \f[CR]%M\f[R]) are expanded as in RTKLIB streams.
\- \f[CR](2)\f[R] \f[CR]:port\f[R] (TCP server) \- \f[CR](3)\f[R] \f[CR]address:port\f[R] (TCP client)
.TP
\f[CR]\-nmea path\f[R]
Output stream path for PVT solutions as NMEA \f[CR]GNRMC\f[R], \f[CR]GNGGA\f[R], and \f[CR]GNGSV\f[R] sentences.
Same path syntax and repeatability as \f[CR]\-log\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]\-rtcm path\f[R]
Output stream path for raw observations and navigation data as RTCM3.3 messages.
Same path syntax and repeatability as \f[CR]\-log\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]\-raw path\f[R]
Output stream path for raw IF data.
Same path syntax and repeatability as \f[CR]\-log\f[R].
Enabled only for Pocket SDR FE or SoapySDR device inputs.
.TP
\f[CR]\-arch nch\f[R]
Number of antenna array channels.
Array CHs are appended after the RF CHs.
[\f[CR]0\f[R]]
.TP
\f[CR]\-geom file\f[R]
Array element positions file (body\-frame, \f[CR]pocket_sdr.py\f[R] array geometry format) applied at startup.
[none]
.TP
\f[CR]\-sens name[,...]\f[R]
Sensors of the RF channels of a SoapySDR device to log every 10 s as \f[CR]$SENS,<time>,<rfch>,<name>,<value>\f[R], e.g.\ \f[CR]temp\f[R], \f[CR]rssi\f[R], \f[CR]lo_locked\f[R] (RF channel) or
\f[CR]ref_locked\f[R] (device) of a USRP.
[\f[CR]temp\f[R]]
.TP
\f[CR]\-h height\f[R]
Console height (rows) for the runtime status display.
[\f[CR]64\f[R]]
.TP
\f[CR]\-opt file\f[R]
System options file.
The recognized keys and defaults are listed below; \f[CR]app/pocket_trk/pocket_trk_default.conf\f[R] provides an example profile.
[none]
.TP
\f[CR]\-debug file\f[R]
Enable RTKLIB trace output to the given file (trace level 3).
.TP
\f[CR]\-v\f[R]
Print version and exit.
.TP
\f[CR][file]\f[R]
Input IF data file path.
If omitted and no \f[CR]\-driver\f[R] is given, the input is taken from a Pocket SDR FE device.
With \f[CR]<file>.tag\f[R] present, format/sampling parameters are auto\-configured.
