.TE
.PP
Assisted acquisition uses the larger of \f[CR]thres_cn0_ext\f[R] and the applicable tracking\-loss threshold plus 1 dB.
L6 tracking uses an internal \f[CR]32.5 dB\-Hz\f[R] loss threshold instead of \f[CR]thres_cn0_u\f[R].
Pilot coherent integration starts only after secondary\-code synchronization; it falls back to per\-code\-period Costas updates if synchronization is lost or \f[CR]b_pll * K * T >= 0.4\f[R], where
\f[CR]K = max(1, round(t_coh / T))\f[R].
.PP
\f[CR]fast_acq = 1\f[R] enables fast acquisition: satellite visibility and Doppler are predicted at the receiver time from the navigation data, almanac, and last FIX position saved in
\f[CR].pocket_navdata.csv\f[R], and satellites predicted below the horizon are skipped.
The receiver time is unknown at start, so the signals are acquired by the full search until the TOW and the week number of a received signal set the receiver time (receiver sync mode
\f[CR]COARSE\f[R], then \f[CR]FINE\f[R] after the first PVT fix, logged as \f[CR]$LOG ... RECEIVER SYNC\f[R]).
The prediction does not use the host PC clock, so it also works for IF data recorded at a different time and for a GNSS simulator.
The last FIX position is inherited regardless of its time.
.PP
All numeric keys other than \f[CR]fftw_wisdom\f[R] are passed to \f[CR]sdr_rcv_setopt()\f[R].
